{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01OJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-integral}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d2cdd54c91172842da7935e351b2e537dfc65808da525fec53dd82898c278104", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c29f2119cac331ae5c1b75ce2f05a23ceb091badf3a6442da39d6ef6ffa82837", "source_text": "A scheme <MATH_0001> is integral if and only if it is reduced and irreducible.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9bb6bbd7811cb17e6dfe0f3e66dd3992c1d6e45eac80ccd16bf7a4f7f2f009d1", "unit_id": "tag:01ON:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01OJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Spec(R) = U \\subset X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$R$", "MATH_0005": "$R$", "MATH_0006": "$(0)$", "MATH_0007": "$R$", "MATH_0008": "$X$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Spec(R) = U \\subset X$", "MATH_0010": "$R$", "MATH_0011": "$X$", "MATH_0012": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-characterize-reduced}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-characterize-reduced}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-characterize-irreducible}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b9acc3382ea343f3f355a3d281d7eca0c187e35f52fe01c2bfe076eace020e58", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bb506a8fcf384263d865e6353c1b876c10bab3a53b0bceca46fb52fc980f88d0", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> is irreducible, then every affine open <MATH_0002>\nis irreducible. If <MATH_0003> is reduced, then <MATH_0004> is reduced, by\nLemma <REF_0001> above. Hence <MATH_0005> is reduced\nand <MATH_0006> is a prime ideal, i.e., <MATH_0007> is an integral domain.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nIf <MATH_0008> is integral, then for every nonempty affine open\n<MATH_0009> the ring <MATH_0010> is reduced\nand hence <MATH_0011> is reduced by Lemma <REF_0002>.\nMoreover, every nonempty affine open is irreducible.\nHence <MATH_0012> is irreducible, see Lemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:476e849e5c4f72ca3208b868b0d3e3e33f18b30e60adba0237cc80c8c8e1f05c", "unit_id": "tag:01ON:proof"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01OJ", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{examples-section-connected-locally-integral-not-integral}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fc33a5734a08dc1d3f5cc72dd410bd275d5dca1cf3502a8269cda0bd6a1ce71a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn Examples, Section\n<REF_0001>\nwe construct a connected affine scheme all of whose local rings are domains,\nbut which is not integral.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:738363d24a599e78d58477b7686fbe27208ff115f3980620084b9300113e0d8a", "unit_id": "tag:01OJ:prose-0001"}
